From 629f6e09598313b9ebf22032ae8ecc6493d30f1a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Codex <codex@openai.com>
Date: Sat, 21 Nov 2026 12:58:49 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] Allow dma-buf imports without the host-pointer extension

Backport the capability separation from steelbrain/metal2vulkan commit
12a8a907bcdd3c7ae5683ee436e83e42fd6397a4 onto the Android fork at
5951098336923a231a011578d8722449a3981034.

Keep pointer import functions and alignment in PointerImport. A device
without that route can still use a caller-supplied dma-buf of the same
pages; a pointer without a usable source keeps its typed refusal. Guard
all pointer-buffer creation, including the older GatherSource API, and
keep existing pointer-capable devices' queries and import behavior.

Add a mock-dispatch regression covering extension presence, pointer
importability and dma-buf availability independently. It checks that a
missing extension is never queried or loaded. Update the host-memory
contract and regenerate the refusal reference.

Verified: 17 focused host-memory tests; targeted runtime clippy with
warnings denied; generated refusal reference check; git diff check.
This is a candidate dependency patch. No Pixel GPU import or iOS boot
was tested. Kernel exporter access, coherent compatible memory types,
internal anonymous allocations and the remaining GPU paths still need
hardware evidence.
